From 6d9855e0d799ecec45d4797cc02908214d8912f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cole Morgan <colerussellmorgan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:42:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] KOReader sync: add Phone (Bluetooth) and Auto sync
 transports on X4 Classic

A Sync Transport setting (Wi-Fi, Phone (Bluetooth), Auto) is stored with
the KOReader sync settings and shown in CrossPoint Sync settings when
FIELD_BLE_SYNC is built in. With Phone, the sync screen stops the page
turner radio, advertises the Field Sync relay, shows the pairing
passkey, runs the usual sync (including Smart sync) over the relay,
then sends bye and stops Bluetooth. Auto tries the saved Wi-Fi for
8 s first. Clipping sync is skipped over Bluetooth.

The x4c environment enables FIELD_BLE_SYNC and keeps NimBLE's
peripheral and broadcaster roles.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
